{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Every clean bird you may eat.</b> But not the unclean — this comes to set a positive command alongside a negative command. And likewise with beasts: ״אֹתָהּ תֹּאכֵלוּ״ — and not an unclean beast. And a negative that emerges from the implication of a positive is [treated as] a positive — so that one transgresses them both as a positive command and as a negative command."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:03.887874476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}